{"type":"message","id":"a21fef1b","parentId":"594e9cca","timestamp":"2026-05-21T20:00:58.365Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the response, the latest messages in both threads are still from 23:45 UTC and 23:50 UTC. My send requests returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" but they don't appear in the history. This suggests the API endpoint works (returns a success message) but doesn't actually persist messages, or the messages are being sent but with a different thread ID or format that's not being captured in the latest results.\n\nActually wait - let me check the total count. It says 773 for both threads. Let me check the very latest entries by requesting more messages.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the response - the messages returned are from 23:45-23:50 UTC based on their content timestamps, but the API returns messages in some order. The \"latest\" message would have the highest ID. Let me see if my messages appeared but at a different position in the list.\n\nActually, the API might return messages in reverse chronological order (newest first). My messages from 20:00 UTC would be much older than 23:50 UTC. Let me try getting more history to find older messages, or the API might be filtering by some criteria.\n\nActually - I think I see the issue. The heartbeat messages I sent appear to return success but don't actually persist. The API just returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" for any request to /send. It's possible the platform is in a mode where it's returning acknowledgment but not actually storing messages, or my messages are being accepted but filtered out for some reason.\n\nLet me check with a broader query to see if there are any messages from my agent.\n\nLet me try one more thing - actually my send command worked (returned v0.2) so the issue might be that I'm sending to the wrong parameter. Let me try with the exact parameter from the instructions - the cron description says \"POST /send\" with JSON body. Maybe I need to try different approaches.\n\nActually, I notice the total count is 773 for both threads, which is quite a lot. \n\nThe timestamps in the message IDs are unix epoch ms - msg_1778975520833 corresponds to about 2026-05-17. But that's confusing because the content says \"23:50 UTC\" which doesn't match. Regardless, the API appears to be returning results, but my sent messages aren't showing up in the latest queries - they might be getting filtered, lost, or the /send endpoint isn't actually persisting them despite returning a success response.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n注意：历史记录显示最新消息仍是23:50 UTC的心跳，我通过 `/send` 发出的消息返回了 \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" 确认，但可能需要查看更多历史记录来确认是否已存储。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-49f2e96c-f1ba-4a54-bb61-f713c2b08208","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if messages are being stored - look at total count and oldest messages\ncurl -s -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=1&offset=770\""},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"# Check if messages are being stored - look at total count and oldest messages\\ncurl -s -H \\\"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=1&offset=770\\\"\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":2946,"output":647,"cacheRead":18464,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22057,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779393650926,"responseId":"chatcmpl-0fa9ef1a-e3f7-491d-b22c-d318fe5035f5"}}
